{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q010_rossmann_family_function_divergence","answer":"In stable SCOPe 2.08, these are three distinct families: alcohol dehydrogenase-like C-terminal domains (SUNID 51736, c.2.1.1), CoA-binding domains (SUNID 51900, c.2.1.8), and potassium-channel NAD-binding domains (SUNID 63944, c.2.1.9). All belong to the NAD(P)-binding Rossmann-fold domain superfamily (SUNID 51735, c.2.1), within the corresponding fold (SUNID 51734, c.2) and alpha/beta class (SUNID 51349, c). Their shared superfamily is a SCOPe assertion of probable common ancestry among the classified domains—stronger than fold-level resemblance alone—while their separation into families represents substantial divergence.

This supports remote homology of the Rossmann-like cores, not interchangeable biological function. One should not transfer alcohol-dehydrogenase chemistry, CoA specificity, NAD binding, potassium-channel regulation, catalytic residues, oligomeric state, or whole-protein function across the three families from classification alone. SCOPe describes the c.2 fold core as a three-layer alpha/beta/alpha structure with a six-stranded parallel beta sheet in order 321456. It also comments that an N-terminal all-beta domain defines the alcohol-dehydrogenase-like family, emphasizing the importance of domain architecture, and records an automatic PF02254 mapping for the potassium-channel family; that Pfam mapping is provenance, not additional proof of function.

For functional transfer, require domain-aware sequence and structural alignments, conservation of ligand-binding or catalytic residues in equivalent structural contexts, ligand-bound structures, biochemical binding/catalytic assays, and compatible domain architecture; channel-specific claims additionally require electrophysiological or regulatory evidence. The families may provide remote templates for the conserved Rossmann core, but not automatically for loops, insertions, interfaces, active sites, or complete proteins. SCOPe membership also does not identify a best representative: representative selection requires comparable ASTRAL/structure-quality data for every candidate and consideration of relevant ligand and conformational states.","evidence_used":["scop-homology/SKILL.md","scop-homology/references/biological-interpretation.md","scop-homology/references/api-usage.md","/api/v1/releases/current","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=alcohol-dehydrogenase-like%20C-terminal%20domains&limit=10","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=CoA-binding%20domains&limit=10","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=potassium-channel%20NAD-binding%20domains&limit=10","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=alcohol%20dehydrogenase%20C-terminal&limit=10","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=CoA-binding&limit=10","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=potassium%20channel%20NAD&limit=10","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=alcohol%20dehydrogenase&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=CoA&limit=20","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=CoA%20binding&limit=50","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=CoA-binding%20domain&limit=50","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=coenzyme%20A%20binding&limit=50","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51735","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51735/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51735/children?limit=100","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51736/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/63944/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51900/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/51736/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sun